  "answer": "Each claim carries one evidence label: implemented | read directly from code at the pinned commit configured | a default, environment variable, packaging or launcher setting tested | exercised by a test in the Lear repository (and, where stated, run on 2026-11-05) inferred | a conclusion drawn from reading the code; no single line proves it Evidence is written `path:Lstart-Lend`, relative to the Lear repository root, at commit `60cf9abf8408`. `python -m ragformation lear docs verify --source <checkout>` re-checks every reference against that commit. [1] They are the knowledge base of the `python -m ragformation lear` assistant, so every factual statement points at the code that supports it. - [implemented] Lear is packaged as the Python distribution `prash-v2` version 0.2.0, requires Python 3.10 or newer, and installs one console script, `prash`, mapped to `prash.cli:main`. [3] Subcommands (14): `run`, `fix`, `investigate`, `stats`, `logs`, `actions`, `audit`, `config`, `circuit`, `watch`, `notify`, `tui`, `repl`, `setup`. [4]",
